    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nThis charming period residence, dating from the late 1800s, is rich in character and presents a wonderful opportunity to create a truly distinctive home. Extended at garden level a number of years ago, the property combines generous proportions with a flexible layout and boasts a superb rear garden.\nAn attractive flight of granite steps leads to the hall door, opening into an impressive entrance hallway. Off this space are two gracious interconnecting reception rooms. The elegant drawing room overlooks Waterloo Road and flows seamlessly into the dining room to the rear. Both rooms retain beautiful period features, including matching fireplaces.\nTo the rear of the hallway lies a bright library/study, complete with a striking glass-panelled staircase leading down to the garden level.\nThe first floor comprises four spacious double bedrooms and a well-appointed family bathroom.\nAt garden level, the property offers extensive open-plan living accommodation running from front to back. This level is also accessible from the front via a practical hallway with excellent storage and cloakroom facilities, as well as a well-appointed shower room featuring a sauna.\nTo the front, a fitted kitchen with a central island and dining area opens into a bright family room, with doors leading out to the rear garden. A fifth bedroom is also located on this level, offering excellent flexibility for guests, a home office, or additional living space.\nThe property is further enhanced by a magnificent sunny rear garden extending to approximately thirty-nine metres, providing a private and tranquil oasis in the heart of the city. To the front, a driveway offers ample off-street parking.\n80 Waterloo Road is presented very well and although the garden level was extended and modernised some years ago, the property does require some modernisation in parts. It is however, an exceptionally spacious family home in a location second to none.\nIdeally situated, this exceptional home enjoys a prime position in the heart of Dublin 4. The location offers enviable convenience, within walking distance of the vibrant amenities of Baggot Street, Ballsbridge, and Donnybrook, as well as the city centre. Nearby Herbert Park provides excellent recreational facilities, while a range of highly regarded primary and secondary schools are nearby. The area is well served by public transport, including numerous bus routes, the DART at Lansdowne Road, and the Aircoach, ensuring easy access to Dublin Airport."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nHall Level - 2m x 8.6m\nSuperb entrance hallway with beautiful period features to include fan light and cornicing. Two interconnecting reception rooms off the hallway and elegant staircase to the first floor.\n\nDrawing Room - 5.6m x 4.2m\nWonderful reception room with sash windows overlooking the Waterloo Road. Attractive marble fireplace with open fire and folding doors lead through to the\n\nDining Room - 4.1m x 5.7m\nLarge picture window overlooking the rear, fireplace with open fire and tiled inset.\n\nLibrary / Study - 2.7m x 3.8m\nGorgeous bright room with built-in shelving unit spotlights, window to side and window to rear.\n\nStaircase - \nGlass panelled staircase leading down to garden level.\n\nFirst Floor - \n\n\nMain Bedroom - 4.3m x 4.6m\nTwo large sash windows overlooking Waterloo Road. Built-in wardrobes and attractive high ceilings.\n\nBedroom - 3m x 4.1m\nSash window overlooking the rear and range built-in wardrobes\n\nBedroom - 2.7m x 4.2m\nDouble bedroom overlooking Waterloo Road.\n\nBedroom - 2.5m x 2.9m\nWindow to the side and back.\n\nFamily Bathroom - \nBath, shower attachment, WC, WHB and shower unit.\n\nGarden Level - \nOffers a strong contemporary family space which connects visually both with the garden and older period house through a light filled atria box via a glass ,timber ,steel staircase .\n\nInner Hallway - 1.8m x 2.7m\nGood storage & cloaks.\n\nFamily Living Space - 4.9m x 7.5m\nTiled floors, gas fire, built-in shelving, and sliding doors opening out to the patio to the rear, bringing the outside into the home.\n\nKitchen / Dining Room - 4.8m 8.5m\nContinuation of tiled floor, modern fitted kitchen with range of appliances, neff double oven, neff hob, sink and two windows overlooking the front of Waterloo Road. Large extractor fan and the integrated appliances.\n\nBedroom 5 - 1.9m x 3.6m\nLocated off the living area this room currently used as a bedroom offers flexible accommodation at garden area,\n\nShower Room - \nGenerous bathroom with tiled floors, tiled walls, large shower unit, separate sauna, WC, whb.\n\nOutside - \nThe rear garden is a particular feature of this fine home. Extending to c. 39m the garden is mainly laid in lawn and has a wonderful sense of space and privacy. There is a patio area outside the sliding doors from the family room and it is a lovely place from which to enjoy al fresco dining. To the front of the property there is a private driveway offering ample off street parking. There are granite steps to the front and steps down to the garden level.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Wonderful period home extending to approximately 285 sq.m / 3,068 sq.ft</li><li> Beautiful period features throughout the property</li><li> A lovely blend of old-world charm and modern accommodation.</li><li> Period feature white marble fireplaces intact with attractive gree glazed tile and wrought iron fire surround .</li><li> Architecturally designed garden level which was extended some years ago.</li><li> Gas fired central heating.</li><li> Superb interconnecting reception rooms</li><li> Shower room with sauna at garden level.</li><li> Excellent rear garden with lawn and patio</li><li> Although now requiring some modernisation in some areas, this is a wonderful spacious family home.</li><li> Spacious driveway providing parking for several cars.</li><li> Security alarm system</li><li> Wonderful versatile accommodation throughout.</ul>"
      },
